      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T21:52:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For typec charger disconnect, i see, this hook is really quick to process, say 1-2 sec while HOOK_POWER_SUPPLY_CHANGE hook from charge_manager_refresh() is taking around some 58-60 sec. The prochot event from ec side is mainly sent for low battery \u0026 charger disconnect events and they must be processed really quickly. So usage of disconnect hook seems relevant here.\nFor charger connect event,we dont send prochot event but just sci event and memmap updation only, so timing for this scenario might not matter much from EC perspective. But, am not sure, if there is any impact at kernel level for overall performance. I feel, it is better to investigate  this timing impact as well, after the entire feature in place and to consider in next optimization stage.",
